# ─── Local customer/scanner/evidence/runtime state ──────────────────
# These paths are never build inputs. Keep this list explicit because an ignored
# local file still enters `docker build` unless it is independently dockerignored.
.local
**/.local
mintvault-scans
**/mintvault-scans
.mintvault-scanner-tools
**/.mintvault-scanner-tools
scans
**/scans
scanner-data
**/scanner-data
scanner-output
**/scanner-output
scanner-runtime
**/scanner-runtime
evidence
**/evidence
runtime-evidence
**/runtime-evidence
backups
**/backups
*.tif
**/*.tif
*.tiff
**/*.tiff
*.raw
**/*.raw
*.dng
**/*.dng
*.heic
**/*.heic
*.heif
**/*.heif

# ─── Standalone local tooling NOT part of the web build ───────────────
# scripts/scanner-app + scripts/scanner-watcher are macOS native scanner
# integrations (LaunchAgents + Electron-style guide window). They talk
# to the server over HTTPS with SCANNER_API_TOKEN — they are not imported
# by the Vite/esbuild build. Excluding almost all of scripts/ saves
# ~513 MB of context per deploy (caught a Fly-builder timeout 2026-05-11).
scripts/*
!scripts/db/
scripts/db/*
!scripts/db/migrate.ts
!scripts/db/lint-destructive-sql.ts
# migrate.ts imports toDirectEndpoint from here (the advisory-lock single-runner guarantee
# connects via the DIRECT endpoint, never the pooler). It is a build-context allowlist, so a
# missing entry does not fail `npm run build` in CI — CI builds the whole repo — it fails only
# inside the Dockerfile, i.e. at deploy time. tests/dockerignore-build-context.test.ts pins it.
!scripts/db/read-only-session.ts

# ─── Project meta / documentation (not needed by build or runtime) ────
docs
attached_assets
**/attached_assets
uploads
**/uploads

# ─── Markdown — keep README, drop everything else at the repo root ────
*.md
!README.md

# Exception: one-off prod migration script needs to reach the build (additive ADD COLUMN x5, see file header)
!scripts/run-mvgs-v2-migration.ts
# Exception: one-off set-designation data repair (dry-run default, see file header)
!scripts/repair-set-designations.ts
# Exception: incident-specific STAGING Canon geometry repair (dry-run default).
# Re-admit only the exact entrypoint; the rest of scripts/staging remains excluded.
!scripts/staging/
scripts/staging/*
!scripts/staging/repair-canon-lide400-geometry.ts
# cornelius-engineering-os:begin id=generated-egress v=1
# Generated engineering intelligence must not enter Docker build context
graphify-out/
.graphify/
# cornelius-engineering-os:end id=generated-egress
